WHAT I HAVE DONE:

1. Basic Security, VLANs, Trunks & Blackhole Ports

Late-night lab session — first pass at securing and segmenting the network.

    Basic Security: Configured hostnames, passwords, and password encryption on all devices.
    VLANs: Separated traffic for each department into its own VLAN.
    Trunks & Blackhole Ports: Fixed trunk link configurations, changed the native VLAN to VLAN 999, and moved all unused switch ports into a dedicated "Blackhole" VLAN to prevent unauthorized access on unassigned ports.

2. EtherChannel & STP Path Optimization

Added link redundancy and bandwidth aggregation across the core and distribution layers, then tuned STP to control path preference.
🔹 EtherChannel

Bundled multiple physical links into single logical links (Port-Channel interfaces) to provide redundancy and increase available bandwidth between switches.
🔹 STP Path Optimization

    Po1 — the EtherChannel between the two distribution switches — was given a lower STP cost, since the distribution layer handles inter-VLAN routing. This keeps Po1 the preferred path whenever possible.
    Po2 — the EtherChannel between the core switches — was left at its default STP cost, serving as a redundant path without a manually forced preference.

🔹 Open Question / Observation

Manually configured spanning-tree cost 1 on the Po1 interface:

    show running-config correctly reflects the configured cost of 1.
    show spanning-tree reports an operational cost of 3.

This discrepancy between configured and operational STP cost on the port-channel is still unresolved — noted here for future investigation.
3. Core Layer Redesign, IP Addressing & Inter-VLAN Routing

Expanded the lab into a full multi-site topology and reworked the core layer.
🔹 Core Layer Redesign

Replaced the HQ core switches with Layer 3 devices (3560), moving away from a pure Layer 2 core to add routing capability above the distribution layer. A practical example of how the "textbook" 3-tier model can be adapted to fit specific design goals.
🔹 IP Addressing

Completed the full IP addressing plan for the network (ISP-side addressing still pending). Extra address space was intentionally reserved at the distribution and core layers to allow for future growth. Note: the subnetting scheme prioritizes clarity and ease of lab work over strict real-world best practices.
🔹 Inter-VLAN Routing

    HQ & Branch 2: Inter-VLAN routing handled via SVIs on the Layer 3 switches.
    Branch 1: Inter-VLAN routing handled via Router-on-a-Stick.

